# DuckDB data files (do not version well data)
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# ...EXCEPT the two WAL-recovery test fixtures. `db.rs`'s resilient_open test include_bytes! them
# at COMPILE time, so with these ignored the whole test suite would not compile from a fresh
# clone (or in CI) — the *.duckdb rule was silently swallowing a tracked build input. They are a
# freshly-created, schema-only project torn mid-write: verified to hold only the DuckDB header and
# create_schema's DDL (table/column names), no well names, field names or log values. Safe to
# version; regenerating a faithful corrupt pair is not reliably reproducible (see the test).
!src-tauri/tests/fixtures/corrupt_torn.duckdb
!src-tauri/tests/fixtures/corrupt_torn.wal

