# Visual Studio IDE cache - was committed by accident (772 MB, incl. a 187 MB
# Copilot index GitHub rejects outright). Regenerated by VS on open; never commit it.
.vs/

# Third-party Claude Code tooling kept beside the repo for convenience, never part of
# the product. model-router (RoboNuggets, CC BY 4.0) is a local plugin marketplace source
# registered at a machine path; vendoring it here would put an attribution-required
# third-party work inside a repo intended to be LICENSED, where neither the generated
# THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md (built from dependency manifests) nor docs/IP_PROVENANCE.md
# would ever record it. Ignored rather than moved because the plugin resolves by path.
model-router/

# The cross-tool evidence corpus - vendor material extracted from IP / Techlog / Geolog
# documentation, cited by thirteen PRD_v2 chapters as a LOCAL reference. CONTRACT.md 2.1
# forbids transcribing vendor material into this tree, and docs/record_parallel_lanes.md
# records the decision to keep it out of git. It was merely untracked, which is not the
# same as settled: git kept offering it, and committing it is NOT cleanly reversible -
# history would carry it until somebody rewrote history and broke every clone. Docs lanes
# get it by cp -r into the worktree; code lanes implement from the committed chapter.
docs/research_2026-08/

# Machine-local agent-tool state. .codex/config.toml hard-codes this repo's absolute path,
# so it is meaningless on any other machine; .castforge/ is one tool's debug + role state.
.castforge/
.codex/

# Design handoff archive - a binary delivered once and unpacked into docs/design_organic/,
# which is the committed authority. Keeping the zip too versions the same content twice,
# one copy of which nothing reads.
SandiBumi UI Redesign.zip
